  "notes": "ETYMOLOGY:\n{対|たい} means facing or opposing, and {峙|じ} means to stand tall (like a peak). Originally described mountains standing face to face, then extended to any opposing forces.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {問題|もんだい}に{対峙|たいじ}する — to confront a problem\n- {敵|てき}と{対峙|たいじ}する — to face off against an enemy\n- {困難|こんなん}に{対峙|たいじ}する — to confront difficulties\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{対決|たいけつ} implies a decisive showdown or battle. {対立|たいりつ} means opposition or conflict between views or groups. {対峙|たいじ} emphasizes the tense state of facing each other, not necessarily fighting.",
